  "adaptations": [
    "PostgreSQL/API remain authoritative for questions, patient state, results and column read/bookmark state; browser content storage omitted.",
    "Model-indexed chat title, literal escaping, revision retries and request cancellation retained.",
    "Name required/no-follow-up default migration preserves custom DB questions and previous intake snapshots; immutable legacy seed retained.",
    "Server stores prompt history and encouragement; base/follow-up/supplemental back routes preserve corrections.",
    "Leave dialog warns that the conversation cannot be resumed; removed upstream claims that persisted reports disappear or reside only in the browser.",
    "Removed stale About sentence saying the trained model will be integrated later.",
    "Atomic result API shows pending loading and completes all steps on response; no fabricated timed model phase progression.",
    "Local font MIME types supported without external font requests.",
    "Font license text is preserved; trailing spaces normalized for repository whitespace checks.",
    "Sent answers appear immediately; the next prompt waits for the server/model response. Retries reconcile with server logs without duplicate bubbles, and internal model-state warnings are not shown in the UI.",
    "User messages and waiting dots paint before requests. Model failures retain the saved pending answer and current prompt; only validated model output advances the conversation, with retry/edit/correction revision checks.",
    "Validated submissions immediately clear textarea/direct-input drafts while retaining the captured answer in the user bubble and retry request.",
    "Latest 29-question defaults migrate only untouched rows; merged help disables default coping while prior intake snapshots and administrator changes remain intact.",
    "Event-dependent examples use validated DB ph_by_option data; UI ownPh/fu/ask metadata is supported without executing DB code. Display fu is distinct from answer follow_up.",
    "Optional yes-detail prompts are shown locally and saved with submitted answers; retries and corrections reconcile prompt/answer pairs without duplicate or obsolete detail prompts.",
    "Question-position encouragement uses 1/3 and 0.66 thresholds. Active draft/answer conversations warn on browser refresh or closing; completed screens do not."
  ]
